{
  "providerId": "dodomain.io",
  "providerName": "DoDomain",
  "serviceId": "dns-records",
  "serviceName": "DNS records",
  "version": 1,
  "logoUrl": "https://dodomain.io/icon.svg",
  "description": "Writes the DNS records a SaaS product needs on its customer's domain when no narrower DoDomain template expresses them, e.g. Amazon SES-style email sending (MX and SPF on a subdomain, several DKIM keys, DMARC) or a site on several subdomains. Every record is a numbered slot in its own group with a fixed record type; host, value, TTL and (MX) priority are variables, and the apply lists exactly the groups it fills, so the consent screen shows only the records being written. TXT slots come in two kinds: txt1..txt8 add a record beside existing ones (conflict mode None), txtr1..txtr4 replace the records a name may hold only one of (DMARC, DKIM keys, MTA-STS, TLS-RPT). SPF is merged through SPFM, never written as a TXT. multiInstance is set because record hosts are variables: re-applying for a second integrator on the same domain must not remove the first one's records. Used by DoDomain (domain-connect-as-a-service) on behalf of its integrator applications.",
  "variableDescription": "For every slot <s> (spf1..spf2, txtr1..txtr4, txt1..txt8, a1..a8, aaaa1..aaaa4, cname1..cname16, mx1..mx5, srv1..srv4, ns1..ns4, caa1..caa2; groupId = <s>): <s>host = the record name relative to the domain, '@' for the domain itself (for SRV, the name after _service._protocol); <s>value = the record value (A/AAAA address, CNAME/MX/NS/SRV target host, TXT data, CAA value such as 0 issue \"letsencrypt.org\"); <s>ttl = the TTL in seconds (not on SPF slots); spf<n>rules = the SPF terms to merge (everything between v=spf1 and the terminal all, e.g. include:amazonses.com); mx<n>priority = the MX preference; srv<n>service, srv<n>protocol, srv<n>priority, srv<n>weight, srv<n>port = the SRV fields. Variables: spf1host, spf1rules, spf2host, spf2rules, txtr1host, txtr1value, txtr1ttl, txtr2host, txtr2value, txtr2ttl, txtr3host, txtr3value, txtr3ttl, txtr4host, txtr4value, txtr4ttl, txt1host, txt1value, txt1ttl, txt2host, txt2value, txt2ttl, txt3host, txt3value, txt3ttl, txt4host, txt4value, txt4ttl, txt5host, txt5value, txt5ttl, txt6host, txt6value, txt6ttl, txt7host, txt7value, txt7ttl, txt8host, txt8value, txt8ttl, a1host, a1value, a1ttl, a2host, a2value, a2ttl, a3host, a3value, a3ttl, a4host, a4value, a4ttl, a5host, a5value, a5ttl, a6host, a6value, a6ttl, a7host, a7value, a7ttl, a8host, a8value, a8ttl, aaaa1host, aaaa1value, aaaa1ttl, aaaa2host, aaaa2value, aaaa2ttl, aaaa3host, aaaa3value, aaaa3ttl, aaaa4host, aaaa4value, aaaa4ttl, cname1host, cname1value, cname1ttl, cname2host, cname2value, cname2ttl, cname3host, cname3value, cname3ttl, cname4host, cname4value, cname4ttl, cname5host, cname5value, cname5ttl, cname6host, cname6value, cname6ttl, cname7host, cname7value, cname7ttl, cname8host, cname8value, cname8ttl, cname9host, cname9value, cname9ttl, cname10host, cname10value, cname10ttl, cname11host, cname11value, cname11ttl, cname12host, cname12value, cname12ttl, cname13host, cname13value, cname13ttl, cname14host, cname14value, cname14ttl, cname15host, cname15value, cname15ttl, cname16host, cname16value, cname16ttl, mx1host, mx1value, mx1priority, mx1ttl, mx2host, mx2value, mx2priority, mx2ttl, mx3host, mx3value, mx3priority, mx3ttl, mx4host, mx4value, mx4priority, mx4ttl, mx5host, mx5value, mx5priority, mx5ttl, srv1host, srv1service, srv1protocol, srv1priority, srv1weight, srv1port, srv1value, srv1ttl, srv2host, srv2service, srv2protocol, srv2priority, srv2weight, srv2port, srv2value, srv2ttl, srv3host, srv3service, srv3protocol, srv3priority, srv3weight, srv3port, srv3value, srv3ttl, srv4host, srv4service, srv4protocol, srv4priority, srv4weight, srv4port, srv4value, srv4ttl, ns1host, ns1value, ns1ttl, ns2host, ns2value, ns2ttl, ns3host, ns3value, ns3ttl, ns4host, ns4value, ns4ttl, caa1host, caa1value, caa1ttl, caa2host, caa2value, caa2ttl.",
